From: mscharged-port
Subject: Offer supersampling and FXAA beside multisampling
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

Antialiasing was only multisampling, which smooths the edges of shapes but
not edges inside textures or alpha-tested surfaces. Two more kinds:
AuroraConfig.sampleShading interpolates every GX vertex output per sample
on multisampled targets, so the fragment shader runs once per sample
(supersampling); AuroraVIOutputConfig.fxaa runs fast approximate
antialiasing over the finished desktop picture before the window copy, so
screenshots show it too. Both are off by default.

